---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/seo';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../config/site';

const path = '/about/';
const title = `About ${SITE_NAME}`;
const description = `${SITE_NAME} is an independent SaaS and AI tool directory focused on real pricing and hidden limits — not sponsored rankings.`;
const schema = [breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About', path }])];
---

<Layout {title} {description} {path} {schema} narrow>
  <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-slate-600" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center">
      <li><a href="/" class="flex min-h-11 min-w-11 items-center justify-center hover:underline">Home</a></li>
      <li aria-hidden="true" class="px-2">/</li>
      <li aria-current="page" class="flex min-h-11 items-center font-medium text-slate-800">About</li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">About {SITE_NAME}</h1>

  <div class="mt-6 space-y-6 rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 leading-relaxed text-slate-700 sm:p-8">
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} is an independent directory of SaaS and AI tools. We focus on the two things buyers usually have to
      dig for: what a tool actually costs once you're past the marketing page, and what limits or gotchas show up
      after you sign up — usage caps, seat minimums, feature gating, and similar fine print.
    </p>

    <p>
      Every tool entry links to the vendor's own website, and we are adding direct links to official pricing
      pages so you can confirm current numbers before you buy. Our <a href="/methodology/" class="font-medium text-indigo-700 hover:underline">methodology
      page</a> explains how pricing and comparisons are put together.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Who this is for</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} is built for people comparing software before they buy: founders and operators picking tools for a
      small team, and anyone trying to work out the real monthly cost of a stack rather than the advertised
      "starting at" price.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">How we keep prices honest</h2>
    <p>
      We only show a price as verified after we have opened the vendor's own pricing page and read the number
      there, in US dollars. For the tools where we have done this, the tool page shows a "Last verified" date and a
      plan table that separates plans for one person from plans for teams, and monthly billing from yearly billing.
      If a number could not be confirmed, we write "Not verified yet" instead of guessing.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tools whose pricing we have not checked yet are still listed, marked as unverified, and are kept out of the
      search engine index until we have verified them. We would rather publish fewer pages we can stand behind than
      many pages with numbers nobody checked.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Where the information comes from</h2>
    <p>
      Prices, plan names, limits and seat minimums come from the vendors' official pricing and help pages. Pros and
      cons, and the short "best for" description, are our own summary of what each tool is designed to do. Tool
      pages answer the questions people ask before buying, such as whether there is a free plan, whether the price is
      per user, and what changes if you pay yearly. Comparison pages put two tools next to each other and show what
      each would cost for a team of one, five and twenty-five people on the starting plan.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Who runs this site</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} is an independent project run by one person. It is not owned by or affiliated with any of the
      vendors listed, there are no paid placements, and no vendor can pay to change a listing. You can reach us at
      any time from the <a href="/contact/" class="font-medium text-indigo-700 hover:underline">contact page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">What we're not</h2>
    <p>
      We're not a review panel with a staff of testers, and we don't run user accounts or a comments system (yet).
      If something on the site is wrong or out of date, the fastest way to fix it is to
      <a href="/contact/" class="font-medium text-indigo-700 hover:underline">tell us</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
